# What semgrep must not scan. This file REPLACES semgrep's built-in defaults, and replacing them
# is the entire reason it exists.
#
# Semgrep ships an implicit ignore list that excludes `tests/` among other things. That is a
# sensible default for a web app, where test code neither ships nor runs anywhere interesting.
# It is the wrong default here, and measurably so: with the built-in list, semgrep scanned 0 of
# the 87 C files under tests/host, and 566 tracked files in total were skipped without the scan
# saying which or why.
#
# tests/ matters in this repository for two reasons:
#
#   1. It runs on every CI runner. `make test`, `make coverage`, `make test-san` and `make fuzz`
#      all compile and execute code from tests/host. A payload placed there executes with the
#      runner's token and network, which makes it a better target than the firmware it tests —
#      and under the default ignore list, nothing would ever look at it.
#   2. It is 18k lines of real C that parses the same wire formats the firmware does, including
#      the fuzz harnesses and the flight-recorder replay path.
#
# So the rule here is: exclude things that are not source we own, and nothing else.

# Build and tool output. Nothing here is written by hand.
build/
build-arm/
site/
workspace/
.venv/
node_modules/
coverage/

# Vendored upstream. deps/dw3000 is the Bruno Randolf DW3000 decadriver (ISC, ~37k lines): it is
# not ours to fix, patching it in place is forbidden by the integration model in CLAUDE.md, and
# its findings would drown everything we can act on. Its supply-chain risk is handled by the
# patch-drift gate, which pins it to a known revision.
deps/dw3000/

# Generated, not authored. twin.js is Emscripten output rebuilt and byte-diffed by the twin-wasm gate;
# docs/architecture is regenerated by `make docs` and never hand-edited.
web-twin/twin.js
docs/architecture/

# Fuzzing corpus: thousands of deliberately malformed binary inputs. Every one of them would
# match something, and that is the point of them.
tests/host/fuzz/corpus/

# Minified third-party assets.
*.min.js
*.min.css

# Binary and media, which no text rule can read.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.ico
*.pdf
*.bin
